{%- doc -%}
  Required acknowledgment of vacation-mode processing delays. A close sibling
  of blocks/return-policy-acknowledgment.liquid, cloned rather than shared so a
  seasonal feature cannot regress the battle-tested final-sale gate. Two
  deliberate differences:

  - All text comes from global theme settings (Vacation Mode group), not block
    settings: the block sits in five product templates and blocks cannot read
    each other's settings, so globals are the single source of truth. The
    whole block is dormant unless `settings.vacation_mode_enabled` is on AND
    `settings.vacation_checkbox_terms` is non-blank.
  - No variant-change untick: the delay applies to every variant equally, so
    silently clearing the box on a size change would be pure friction.

  Preserved mechanics:

  - A required checkbox bound to the product form via `form="..."`, so native
    HTML5 submit-time validation blocks Add to Cart until ticked. The terms
    div is the checkbox's `aria-describedby`: the label is short and does not
    carry the meaning on its own.
  - Records the acknowledgment as a line-item property under the
    merchant-editable `settings.vacation_property_label` key (escaped: the
    label is operator text and must not be able to malform the input's name
    attribute). The value embeds `settings.vacation_processing_date` ("Yes -
    processing begins after August 15") so each order records the exact date
    the customer acknowledged; blank date falls back to plain "Yes". For
    support-ticket triage, not a click-wrap contract.
  - Renders its validation message as visible `role="alert"` text with
    `aria-invalid` and an `aria-describedby` append, because the native bubble
    alone does not satisfy WCAG 3.3.1.
  - Hides the accelerated-checkout container while unticked via a fail-closed
    `data-vacation-pending` `:has()` rule (documented in
    blocks/accelerated-checkout.liquid). Composes with the return-policy gate:
    each rule independently hides the same container, so it shows only when
    neither acknowledgment is pending.
  - Window capture-phase interception of the sticky add-to-cart puppet click,
    which must stay even though return-policy also provides one: templates
    without the return-policy block (shift-fuel) have no other interceptor,
    and double interception is benign since both call whole-form
    reportValidity().

  The schema declares `"tag": null` and this file emits its own
  `<vacation-acknowledgment-component>` root: a schema-generated tag renders
  even when the block body is empty, and the fail-closed `:has()` rule would
  match that empty element and hide accelerated checkout with no checkbox
  present to ever un-hide it. Do not move the element back into the schema's
  `tag`.

  This block depends on a sibling `buy-buttons` block in the same section: the
  `product_form_id` is derived from the section id
  (`BuyButtons-ProductForm-{section.id}`) and the `<product-form-component>`
  element is queried within the section root by JS.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign block_settings = block.settings
  assign product_form_id = 'BuyButtons-ProductForm-' | append: section.id
  assign element_id = 'VacationAck-' | append: block.id
  assign terms_id = 'VacationAckTerms-' | append: block.id
  assign error_id = 'VacationAckError-' | append: block.id
  assign label_text = settings.vacation_checkbox_label
  assign terms = settings.vacation_checkbox_terms

  assign product_resource = closest.product

  comment
    The property label is operator-editable global text; escape it so quotes
    or brackets cannot malform the input's name attribute. The value carries
    the specific processing date the customer acknowledged
    (settings.vacation_processing_date), so orders record which date was
    agreed to; with the date setting blank it degrades to a plain Yes.
  endcomment
  assign property_label = settings.vacation_property_label | strip | default: 'Delayed processing acknowledged' | escape
  assign property_name = 'properties[' | append: property_label | append: ']'
  assign processing_date = settings.vacation_processing_date | strip
  if processing_date == blank
    assign ack_value = 'products.product.vacation_acknowledgment_value' | t
  else
    assign ack_value = 'products.product.vacation_acknowledgment_value_dated' | t: date: processing_date
  endif
  comment
    The date is operator text and the checkbox snippet emits value="{{ value }}"
    verbatim; escape so a stray quote cannot break out of the attribute.
  endcomment
  assign ack_value = ack_value | escape
-%}

{%- if settings.vacation_mode_enabled and terms != blank -%}
  <vacation-acknowledgment-component
    class="spacing-style"
    style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: block_settings %}"
    data-product-id="{{ product_resource.id }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div id="{{ terms_id }}" class="vacation-acknowledgment__terms">{{ settings.vacation_checkbox_terms }}</div>

    {% render 'checkbox',
      name: property_name,
      value: ack_value,
      label: label_text,
      id: element_id,
      checked: false,
      events: 'on:change="/handleChange"',
      disabled: false,
      required: true,
      formId: product_form_id,
      inputRef: 'checkbox',
      describedBy: terms_id
    %}

    {%- comment -%}
      The visible error message. Empty until JS fills it, so it never occupies
      space or announces on a valid form. `role="alert"` announces the moment
      it is filled; the JS pairs it with `aria-invalid` on the checkbox and
      appends this id to the checkbox's `aria-describedby`.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p
      id="{{ error_id }}"
      class="vacation-acknowledgment__error"
      ref="errorMessage"
      role="alert"
      hidden
    ></p>

    {%- comment -%}
      Translated string source for JS. Permanently hidden; the JS reads
      textContent.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span hidden ref="invalidMessage">
      {{- 'products.product.vacation_acknowledgment_invalid' | t | escape -}}
    </span>

    <noscript>
      <style>
        product-form-component [ref="acceleratedCheckoutButtonContainer"] { display: none; }
      </style>
    </noscript>
  </vacation-acknowledgment-component>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  vacation-acknowledgment-component {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
  }

  vacation-acknowledgment-component .vacation-acknowledgment__terms {
    margin-block-end: var(--padding-sm);
    font-size: var(--font-size--xs);
  }

  vacation-acknowledgment-component .vacation-acknowledgment__terms p {
    margin-block: 0 var(--padding-sm);
  }

  vacation-acknowledgment-component .vacation-acknowledgment__error {
    margin-block: var(--padding-xs) 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size--xs);
    color: var(--color-error, currentcolor);
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  vacation-acknowledgment-component .vacation-acknowledgment__error[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /*
   * The shared checkbox snippet ships with white-space: nowrap +
   * text-overflow: ellipsis on .checkbox__label-text; the label here is
   * operator-editable, so keep the wrap override. Matches
   * blocks/return-policy-acknowledgment.liquid.
   */
  vacation-acknowledgment-component .checkbox__label {
    align-items: flex-start;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-block-start: var(--padding-sm);
  }

  vacation-acknowledgment-component .checkbox__label-text {
    white-space: normal;
    overflow: visible;
    text-overflow: clip;
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  /*
   * Cross-block gate. Fail-closed: matches whenever the component does NOT
   * have data-vacation-pending='false', covering both the pre-JS state and
   * the unchecked state. Independent of (and composing with) the
   * return-policy gate on the same container: accelerated checkout shows
   * only when no pending acknowledgment remains.
   *
   * Cross-block dependency: targets the accelerated-checkout container by
   * its `ref` attribute (see blocks/accelerated-checkout.liquid). Renaming
   * the ref will silently disable the gate.
   */
  .shopify-section:has(
    vacation-acknowledgment-component:not([data-vacation-pending='false'])
  ) [ref='acceleratedCheckoutButtonContainer'] {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

<script
  src="{{ 'vacation-acknowledgment.js' | asset_url }}"
  type="module"
  fetchpriority="low"
></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.vacation_acknowledgment",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:content.padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "t:settings.top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "t:settings.bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-inline-start", "label": "t:settings.left", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-inline-end", "label": "t:settings.right", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "t:names.vacation_acknowledgment", "category": "t:categories.product" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
